Z||000004||Sillhouette.com||05-10-2000||04:43 PM||||The nicest seats I saw for a fiero is the ones that get reupholstered by RSM.  They are also able to change the foamy material that sometimes flattens. If you want to add extra padding to your satisfaction thats ok too.  Forgot to mention that color is another option that is up to you....<P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||05-10-2000||04:56 PM||||the Clubmans are LIGHT! thats why i got them.. was looking for lighter, better faster more. but a few months later i realized... i'm safer with this harness yes.. but it takes 10 minutes to buckle up and get in the car.. if you leave your keys in your pocket you have to get out of the car to get them... For a NICE light sport seat contact Jamex  at either <A HREF="http://www.jamex.nl" TARGET=_blank>www.jamex.nl</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.jamex.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jamex.com</A>   or springguys@aol.com comfy and functional. and not sore forming. I'll find the pic of them in my car and repost it... I've ditched the racing seats for COMFY firebird seats with a regular seat belt... I'm over the lighter kick i was on... no tunes is a pain.. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||05-10-2000||05:02 PM||||the reason i didn't get the Forzas.. they are to wide.. they rub on the door and you can't roll up the window the head restraints will break the window... special thanks to AutoMOD here in atlanta for loaning me 4 different Corbeaus for proper fit. yes they have nice seat tracks but their intended for the clubmans... I just transfered them to my firebird seats and was gunna keep the Corbeaus for show only but a Civic buddy of mine wanted um.. heheheh he paid me more than I paid for them...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  he still saved money though. ||||reg||1
